WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.420
A bare stage, five acts along the bottom.

2
00:00:03.470 --> 00:00:07.110
Centre stage, a robed figure: Caesar.

3
00:00:07.160 --> 00:00:11.145
At the midpoint, Act 3,
he cries out: "Et tu,

4
00:00:11.195 --> 00:00:13.610
Brute?—Then fall, Caesar!"

5
00:00:13.660 --> 00:00:15.570
The lights on him go dark.

6
00:00:15.620 --> 00:00:19.590
Brutus stays in the light,
through Act 4 and Act 5.

7
00:00:19.640 --> 00:00:23.800
The play is called Julius Caesar,
and he dies halfway through.

8
00:00:23.850 --> 00:00:25.690
So whose tragedy is it?

9
00:00:25.740 --> 00:00:28.700
In this mission, you'll
walk through all five acts,

10
00:00:28.750 --> 00:00:31.940
from the Ides of March to
the battlefield at Philippi.

11
00:00:31.990 --> 00:00:36.000
You'll see why Shakespeare puts the
murder right at the centre of the play.

12
00:00:36.050 --> 00:00:40.090
And you'll learn what a tragedy is:
a great figure brought to death,

13
00:00:40.140 --> 00:00:42.460
partly through their own choices.

14
00:00:42.510 --> 00:00:46.190
Your mission: decide whose
tragedy this really is.
